# Firebase Auth sign-in helper, served from OUR origin so the handshake is FIRST-PARTY.
# Firebase normally serves these from <project>.firebaseapp.com, but a cross-origin helper is
# exactly what Safari's storage partitioning breaks: the redirect comes back and the credential
# cannot be read out, so the installed iOS app can never finish signing in. Same-origin removes
# the third party entirely. See docs/runbooks/firebase-auth-helper-selfhost.md.
#
# The helper must answer on EXTENSIONLESS paths (Firebase's own URLs), while the files carry
# .html so the host sends `Content-Type: text/html` without any per-path header override — a
# browser will not execute an HTML document served as octet-stream. These rewrites bridge the
# two, and MUST stay above the SPA fallback: the first matching rule wins, so the catch-all
# below would otherwise hand Google's redirect our index.html instead of the handler.
/__/auth/handler   /__/auth/handler.html   200
/__/auth/iframe    /__/auth/iframe.html    200
/__/auth/links     /__/auth/links.html     200

# SPA fallback
/*    /index.html   200
